      "dc.description.abstract": [
        {
          "value": "Recently, sparse coding has been widely adopted for data representation in real-world applications. In order to consider the geometric structure of data, we propose a novel method, local and global regularized sparse coding (LGSC), for data representation. LGSC not only models the global geometric structure by a global regression regularizer, but also takes into account the manifold structure using a local regression regularizer. Compared with traditional sparse coding methods, the proposed method can preserve both global and local geometric structures of the original high-dimensional data in a new representation space. Experimental results on benchmark datasets show that the proposed method can improve the performance of clustering.",
          "language": null,
          "authority": null,
          "confidence": -1,
          "place": 0
        }
      ],
